QUESTION_BANK.push(
{id:113,section:"RW",unitId:"u-info",domain:"Information and Ideas",skill:"Inferences",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",p:"In a study, bees were trained to link lemon scent with sugar water. When the sugar was removed, most bees still visited lemon-scented flowers for several days. This suggests that the bees' behavior",q:"Which choice most logically completes the text?",o:["was a learned association that did not disappear immediately", "depended entirely on the presence of sugar", "shows that bees cannot tell scents apart", "proves that bees prefer lemon to every other scent"],c:0,e:"The bees kept visiting lemon-scented flowers after the sugar was gone, so the link they learned lasted for a while. B contradicts the result. C is not supported: they clearly told lemon apart. D overreaches: only lemon was tested.",e_ru:"Пчёлы продолжали лететь на запах лимона и без сахара, значит выученная связь сохранялась. B противоречит результату, C не следует из текста, D — слишком сильный вывод: проверяли только лимон.",t:"A valid inference stays close to the evidence and does not overreach.",t_ru:"Верный вывод опирается на данные и не выходит за их пределы.",reviewed:true},
{id:114,section:"RW",unitId:"u-info",domain:"Information and Ideas",skill:"Main idea",difficulty:"Easy",type:"mc",p:"Urban rooftop gardens do more than supply vegetables. They lower building temperatures by shading roofs, absorb rainwater that would otherwise overload drains, and give residents a shared space to meet. Cities that treat them as decoration miss most of what they offer.",q:"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?",o:["Rooftop gardens offer several benefits beyond growing food.", "Rooftop gardens are mainly decorative.", "Rooftop gardens overload city drains.", "Vegetables grow poorly on rooftops."],c:0,e:"The text lists cooling, rainwater absorption and a shared space, then says treating gardens as decoration misses most of their value. A covers all of this. B is the view the text criticizes; C reverses the drainage point; D is never claimed.",e_ru:"В тексте перечислены охлаждение, поглощение дождевой воды и общее пространство. Вариант A охватывает всё. B — позиция, которую текст критикует, C искажает мысль о дренаже, D не упоминается.",t:"The main idea covers the whole text, not just one detail.",t_ru:"Главная мысль охватывает весь текст, а не одну деталь.",reviewed:true},
{id:115,section:"RW",unitId:"u-craft",domain:"Craft and Structure",skill:"Text structure",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",p:"Dr. Lena Ortiz spent a decade documenting how coral reefs recover after storms. She found that reefs with diverse fish populations regrew faster than those dominated by a single species. Her results suggest that protecting biodiversity may be a practical way to strengthen reef resilience.",q:"What is the main function of the final sentence?",o:["It interprets the finding as a possible conservation strategy.", "It casts doubt on the study's methods.", "It introduces an unrelated topic.", "It repeats the first sentence."],c:0,e:"The last sentence moves from the result (diverse reefs regrew faster) to what it might mean for practice. B and C have no basis in the text; D is wrong because the first sentence describes the research, not its implication.",e_ru:"Последнее предложение переходит от результата к возможному практическому выводу. B и C ничем не подтверждены, а первое предложение описывает исследование, а не вывод.",t:"Ask what a sentence does (describes, explains, concludes), not only what it says.",t_ru:"Спрашивайте, что делает предложение (описывает, объясняет, делает вывод), а не только о чём оно.",reviewed:true},
{id:116,section:"RW",unitId:"u-trans",domain:"Expression of Ideas",skill:"Transitions",difficulty:"Easy",type:"mc",p:"The museum replaced its printed labels with touch screens. ____ visitors now spend longer at each display.",q:"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?",o:["For instance,", "As a result,", "Nevertheless,", "Meanwhile,"],c:1,e:"Replacing labels with touch screens is the cause; visitors staying longer is the effect, so 'As a result' fits. 'Nevertheless' signals contrast, 'For instance' an example, 'Meanwhile' a simultaneous but unrelated event.",e_ru:"Замена подписей экранами — причина, а то, что посетители дольше задерживаются, — следствие, поэтому подходит «As a result». Остальные связки обозначают контраст, пример или параллельное событие.",t:"Name the relationship (cause, contrast, example) before choosing the transition.",t_ru:"Сначала определите связь (причина, контраст, пример), потом выбирайте слово.",reviewed:true},
{id:117,section:"RW",unitId:"u-bounds",domain:"Standard English Conventions",skill:"Sentence boundaries",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",p:"The festival offers workshops in painting, pottery, and ___ may join only two per day.",q:"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to Standard English?",o:["weaving, participants", "weaving; participants", "weaving participants", "weaving, so, participants"],c:1,e:"Both parts are complete sentences, so they need a semicolon (or a period). A is a comma splice, C a run-on, D misuses commas around 'so'.",e_ru:"Обе части — самостоятельные предложения, поэтому нужна точка с запятой. A — запятая вместо границы, C — слитное предложение, D — лишние запятые.",t:"Two independent clauses need a period, a semicolon, or a comma plus a conjunction.",t_ru:"Два самостоятельных предложения разделяют точкой, точкой с запятой или запятой с союзом.",reviewed:true},
{id:118,section:"RW",unitId:"u-form",domain:"Standard English Conventions",skill:"Subject-verb agreement",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",p:"The list of required books, which includes three novels and two plays, ___ posted outside the office.",q:"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to Standard English?",o:["were","are","have been","has been"],c:3,e:"The subject is 'list' (singular), not 'novels' or 'plays'. The phrase between the commas only adds information. A singular subject takes 'has been'; the other options are plural.",e_ru:"Подлежащее — «list» (единственное число), а не «novels» или «plays». Вставка между запятыми только добавляет информацию. Единственному числу соответствует «has been», остальные варианты — множественное число.",t:"Ignore the phrase between commas when finding the subject.",t_ru:"Не учитывайте вставку между запятыми, когда ищете подлежащее.",reviewed:true},
{id:119,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-alg",domain:"Algebra",skill:"Linear equations & Systems",difficulty:"Easy",type:"mc",q:"A line passes through (0, 4) and (2, 10). What is its slope?",o:["2", "3", "5", "6"],c:1,e:"Slope = change in y / change in x = (10 − 4)/(2 − 0) = 3. A is the x-change only, C is 10/2, D is the y-change only.",e_ru:"Наклон = (10 − 4)/(2 − 0) = 3. A — только изменение x, C — 10/2, D — только изменение y.",t:"Slope is rise over run: (y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁).",t_ru:"Наклон — это приращение y, делённое на приращение x.",reviewed:true},
{id:120,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-alg",domain:"Algebra",skill:"Linear equations & Systems",difficulty:"Medium",type:"spr",q:"If 3(x − 2) = 2x + 5, what is x? (Enter a number)",ans:["11"],e:"Expand: 3x − 6 = 2x + 5. Subtract 2x: x − 6 = 5. Add 6: x = 11. Check: 3(9) = 27 and 2(11) + 5 = 27.",e_ru:"Раскрываем скобки: 3x − 6 = 2x + 5, значит x = 11. Проверка: 3·9 = 27 и 2·11 + 5 = 27.",t:"Expand, collect x on one side, then check by substitution.",t_ru:"Раскройте скобки, соберите x в одной части и проверьте подстановкой.",reviewed:true},
{id:121,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-alg",domain:"Algebra",skill:"Linear equations & Systems",difficulty:"Hard",type:"mc",q:"How many solutions does 4x + 6 = 2(2x + 3) have?",o:["No solution", "Exactly one", "Exactly two", "Infinitely many"],c:3,e:"The right side expands to 4x + 6, so both sides are identical and every x works. 'No solution' would need different constants; 'exactly one' needs different x-coefficients.",e_ru:"Правая часть равна 4x + 6, обе части совпадают, поэтому подходит любое x. Без решений было бы при разных константах, одно решение — при разных коэффициентах.",t:"Same slope and same intercept: infinitely many solutions.",t_ru:"Одинаковый наклон и свободный член дают бесконечно много решений.",reviewed:true},
{id:122,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-adv",domain:"Advanced Math",skill:"Quadratics & Exponential functions",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",q:"What is the sum of the solutions of x² − 5x + 6 = 0?",o:["5", "6", "−5", "1"],c:0,e:"Factor: (x − 2)(x − 3) = 0, so x = 2 or 3, and the sum is 5. B is the product, C has the wrong sign, D is the difference.",e_ru:"Раскладываем: (x − 2)(x − 3) = 0, корни 2 и 3, сумма 5. B — произведение, C — неверный знак, D — разность.",t:"For x² + bx + c = 0 the roots sum to −b.",t_ru:"Для x² + bx + c = 0 сумма корней равна −b.",reviewed:true},
{id:123,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-adv",domain:"Advanced Math",skill:"Quadratics & Exponential functions",difficulty:"Hard",type:"spr",q:"If f(x) = 2^x + 3, what is f(4) − f(1)? (Enter a number)",ans:["14"],e:"f(4) = 16 + 3 = 19 and f(1) = 2 + 3 = 5, so the difference is 14. The constant 3 cancels.",e_ru:"f(4) = 16 + 3 = 19, f(1) = 2 + 3 = 5, разность 14. Константа 3 сокращается.",t:"Evaluate each value separately, then subtract.",t_ru:"Вычислите значения отдельно и потом вычтите.",reviewed:true},
{id:124,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-data",domain:"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis",skill:"Ratios, Percentages & Statistics",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",q:"A bag has 4 red, 6 blue and 5 green marbles. One marble is chosen at random. What is the probability it is not blue?",o:["2/5", "3/5", "4/15", "9/10"],c:1,e:"There are 15 marbles and 9 are not blue, so 9/15 = 3/5. A is the probability of blue, C counts only red, D uses the wrong denominator.",e_ru:"Всего 15 шаров, не синих 9: 9/15 = 3/5. A — вероятность синего, C — только красные, D — неверный знаменатель.",t:"P(not A) = 1 − P(A); count outcomes carefully.",t_ru:"P(не A) = 1 − P(A); аккуратно считайте исходы.",reviewed:true},
{id:125,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-data",domain:"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis",skill:"Ratios, Percentages & Statistics",difficulty:"Medium",type:"spr",q:"A car travels 150 miles on 5 gallons of fuel. At the same rate, how many gallons are needed for 330 miles? (Enter a number)",ans:["11"],e:"The rate is 150/5 = 30 miles per gallon, so 330 miles need 330/30 = 11 gallons.",e_ru:"Расход: 150/5 = 30 миль на галлон, значит на 330 миль нужно 330/30 = 11 галлонов.",t:"Find the unit rate first, then scale.",t_ru:"Сначала найдите единичную ставку, потом масштабируйте.",reviewed:true},
{id:126,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-geom",domain:"Geometry and Trigonometry",skill:"Triangles, Circles & Area/Volume",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",q:"Triangle ABC is similar to triangle DEF, with AB = 6, DE = 9 and BC = 8. What is EF?",o:["10", "11", "12", "18"],c:2,e:"The scale factor is 9/6 = 1.5, so EF = 8 × 1.5 = 12. B adds 3 instead of multiplying; D doubles 9.",e_ru:"Коэффициент подобия 9/6 = 1,5, значит EF = 8 × 1,5 = 12. B — прибавление вместо умножения, D — удвоение 9.",t:"Similar figures scale by a constant factor (multiply, not add).",t_ru:"Подобные фигуры связаны постоянным множителем (умножение, а не сложение).",reviewed:true}
);
QUESTION_BANK.push(
{id:127,section:"RW",unitId:"u-info",domain:"Information and Ideas",skill:"Evidence",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",p:"A student claims that urban trees reduce summer temperatures on city streets.",q:"Which finding, if true, most directly supports the student's claim?",o:["Streets lined with trees were on average 3°C cooler in summer than similar streets without trees.", "Many cities plant new trees every spring.", "Trees absorb carbon dioxide from the air.", "Residents enjoy walking beneath trees."],c:0,e:"The claim is about street temperature. Only A reports a temperature difference tied to trees. B, C and D may be true but say nothing about temperature.",e_ru:"Утверждение о температуре улиц. Только A сообщает о разнице температур из-за деревьев. B, C и D могут быть верны, но о температуре не говорят.",t:"Evidence must address the exact claim, not just the same topic.",t_ru:"Доказательство должно относиться именно к утверждению, а не просто к теме.",reviewed:true},
{id:128,section:"RW",unitId:"u-craft",domain:"Craft and Structure",skill:"Words in context",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",p:"The author's account of the negotiation was ______; it included every detail, even those that made her own role look less impressive.",q:"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?",o:["candid", "vague", "hostile", "ornate"],c:0,e:"She included every detail, even unflattering ones, which means she was frank: 'candid'. 'Vague' is the opposite, and nothing suggests hostility or elaborate decoration.",e_ru:"Она включила все детали, даже невыгодные, то есть была откровенна: «candid». «Vague» — противоположность, а враждебности или украшательства в тексте нет.",t:"Use the clues in the sentence to predict the word before reading the options.",t_ru:"Предскажите слово по подсказкам в предложении до просмотра вариантов.",reviewed:true},
{id:129,section:"RW",unitId:"u-form",domain:"Standard English Conventions",skill:"Verb tense",difficulty:"Easy",type:"mc",p:"By the time the guests arrived, the chef ___ the main course.",q:"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to Standard English?",o:["finishes", "had finished", "will finish", "finishing"],c:1,e:"'By the time the guests arrived' sets a past point, and the cooking happened earlier, so the past perfect 'had finished' is needed.",e_ru:"«By the time the guests arrived» задаёт момент в прошлом, а готовка закончилась раньше, поэтому нужно past perfect: «had finished».",t:"An action completed before another past action takes the past perfect.",t_ru:"Действие, завершённое раньше другого прошлого действия, ставится в past perfect.",reviewed:true},
{id:130,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-alg",domain:"Algebra",skill:"Linear equations & Systems",difficulty:"Easy",type:"spr",q:"If x + y = 10 and x − y = 4, what is x? (Enter a number)",ans:["7"],e:"Add the equations: 2x = 14, so x = 7 (and y = 3).",e_ru:"Сложим уравнения: 2x = 14, значит x = 7 (и y = 3).",t:"Adding equations can eliminate a variable.",t_ru:"Сложение уравнений может исключить переменную.",reviewed:true},
{id:131,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-adv",domain:"Advanced Math",skill:"Quadratics & Exponential functions",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",q:"Which expression is equivalent to (x + 3)²?",o:["x² + 9", "x² + 6x + 9", "x² + 3x + 9", "2x + 6"],c:1,e:"(x + 3)² = (x + 3)(x + 3) = x² + 6x + 9. A forgets the middle term, C halves it, D is 2(x + 3).",e_ru:"(x + 3)² = x² + 6x + 9. A теряет средний член, C берёт его вдвое меньше, D — это 2(x + 3).",t:"Squaring a binomial always creates a middle term 2ab.",t_ru:"При возведении двучлена в квадрат всегда появляется средний член 2ab.",reviewed:true},
{id:132,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-data",domain:"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis",skill:"Ratios, Percentages & Statistics",difficulty:"Easy",type:"spr",q:"What is the mean of the data set 2, 4, 4, 6, 9? (Enter a number)",ans:["5"],e:"The sum is 2 + 4 + 4 + 6 + 9 = 25, and there are 5 values, so the mean is 25/5 = 5.",e_ru:"Сумма 2 + 4 + 4 + 6 + 9 = 25, значений 5, среднее 25/5 = 5.",t:"Mean = sum ÷ count.",t_ru:" Среднее = сумма ÷ количество.",reviewed:true}
);
QUESTION_BANK.push(
{id:133,section:"RW",unitId:"u-bounds",domain:"Standard English Conventions",skill:"Commas",difficulty:"Easy",type:"mc",q:"After the storm ___ volunteers began to clear the road.",o:["passed the","passed, the","passed; the","passed: the"],c:1,e:"\"After the storm passed\" is an introductory clause that cannot stand alone. A comma separates it from the main clause that follows. A semicolon or colon would need a complete sentence before it.",e_ru:"«After the storm passed» — вводная часть, которая не может стоять отдельно. Запятая отделяет её от главной части. Точке с запятой или двоеточию нужно законченное предложение перед ними.",t:"Put a comma after an introductory clause.",t_ru:"После вводной части ставьте запятую.",reviewed:true},
{id:134,section:"RW",unitId:"u-bounds",domain:"Standard English Conventions",skill:"Sentence boundaries",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",q:"The road was closed ___ we took the longer route.",o:["; as a result,",", as a result,","as a result,",". as a result,"],c:0,e:"Both parts are complete sentences, so a semicolon is needed, and the transition \"as a result\" takes a comma after it. A comma alone makes a comma splice, no punctuation makes a run-on, and a period must be followed by a capital letter.",e_ru:"Обе части — законченные предложения, поэтому нужна точка с запятой, а после «as a result» — запятая. Одна запятая даёт comma splice, без знака получится слитное предложение, а после точки нужна заглавная буква.",t:"A transition between two complete sentences follows a semicolon or period and is followed by a comma.",t_ru:"Переход между двумя законченными предложениями ставят после точки с запятой или точки, а после него — запятая.",reviewed:true},
{id:135,section:"RW",unitId:"u-form",domain:"Standard English Conventions",skill:"Subject-verb agreement",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",q:"Neither the manager nor the employees ___ aware of the change.",o:["was","is","were","has been"],c:2,e:"With \"neither ... nor\", the verb agrees with the subject closest to it. That is \"employees\", which is plural, so \"were\" is correct. The other options are singular.",e_ru:"В конструкции «neither ... nor» глагол согласуется с ближайшим подлежащим. Это «employees», множественное число, поэтому «were». Остальные варианты — единственное число.",t:"With neither/nor, match the verb to the nearer subject.",t_ru:"С neither/nor согласуйте глагол с ближайшим подлежащим.",reviewed:true},
{id:136,section:"RW",unitId:"u-form",domain:"Standard English Conventions",skill:"Possessives",difficulty:"Easy",type:"mc",q:"The two ___ lunch boxes were left in the classroom.",o:["students'","student's","students","students's"],c:0,e:"\"Two\" shows there is more than one student, and the lunch boxes belong to them. The plural possessive is \"students'\". \"Student's\" is singular, \"students\" shows no ownership, and \"students's\" is not standard.",e_ru:"«Two» показывает, что студентов несколько, и коробки принадлежат им. Форма притяжательного множественного числа — «students'». «Student's» — единственное число, «students» не показывает принадлежность, «students's» не используется.",t:"For a plural noun ending in -s, add only an apostrophe to show possession.",t_ru:"К существительному во множественном числе на -s для принадлежности добавляют только апостроф.",reviewed:true},
{id:137,section:"RW",unitId:"u-craft",domain:"Craft and Structure",skill:"Words in context",difficulty:"Easy",type:"mc",p:"The scientist's tone was ___; she neither praised nor criticized the results, simply reporting them.",q:"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?",o:["neutral","enthusiastic","hostile","sentimental"],c:0,e:"The clue is \"neither praised nor criticized\": she took no side, which is what \"neutral\" means. \"Enthusiastic\" implies praise, \"hostile\" implies criticism, and \"sentimental\" means driven by emotion.",e_ru:"Подсказка — «neither praised nor criticized»: она не занимала ничью сторону, то есть была «neutral». «Enthusiastic» подразумевает похвалу, «hostile» — критику, «sentimental» — эмоциональность.",t:"Find the clue in the sentence that defines the missing word.",t_ru:"Найдите в предложении подсказку, которая определяет пропущенное слово.",reviewed:true},
{id:138,section:"RW",unitId:"u-trans",domain:"Expression of Ideas",skill:"Transitions",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",p:"Most plants need sunlight to grow. ___, some fungi thrive in complete darkness.",q:"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?",o:["In contrast","For instance","As a result","Likewise"],c:0,e:"The second sentence describes something that differs from the first: plants need light, but fungi do not. \"In contrast\" signals this. \"For instance\" introduces an example, \"as a result\" a consequence, and \"likewise\" a similarity.",e_ru:"Второе предложение описывает отличие от первого: растениям нужен свет, а грибам нет. Это показывает «In contrast». «For instance» вводит пример, «as a result» — следствие, «likewise» — сходство.",t:"Decide first whether the ideas contrast, agree, or follow from each other.",t_ru:"Сначала решите: идеи противопоставлены, согласуются или вытекают одна из другой.",reviewed:true},
{id:139,section:"RW",unitId:"u-trans",domain:"Expression of Ideas",skill:"Concision",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",q:"Which choice is the most concise way to express the idea without losing meaning? \"The reason that he was late was because the bus broke down.\"",o:["He was late because the bus broke down.","The reason he was late is due to the fact that the bus broke down.","The cause of his lateness was the bus having broke down.","He was late for the reason of the bus breaking down."],c:0,e:"Choice A says everything in the fewest words. The others repeat the idea of cause (\"reason ... because\", \"due to the fact that\") or add awkward wording. C also uses \"broke\" instead of \"broken\".",e_ru:"Вариант A передаёт всё меньшим числом слов. В остальных причина повторяется («reason ... because», «due to the fact that») или фраза звучит громоздко. В C ещё и «broke» вместо «broken».",t:"Cut words that repeat an idea already expressed.",t_ru:"Убирайте слова, которые повторяют уже выраженную мысль.",reviewed:true},
{id:140,section:"RW",unitId:"u-info",domain:"Information and Ideas",skill:"Main idea",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",p:"A new analysis of tree rings from northern forests shows that growth slowed during years of unusually warm summers, contradicting the assumption that warmer weather always helps trees grow.",q:"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?",o:["Warm summers do not always make trees grow faster.","Tree rings cannot be used to measure growth.","Northern forests are disappearing.","Trees grow fastest in cold weather."],c:0,e:"The text says growth slowed in unusually warm summers, which challenges the belief that warmth always helps. A states exactly this. B contradicts the use of tree rings, C is never mentioned, and D goes beyond the evidence.",e_ru:"В тексте сказано, что рост замедлялся в необычно тёплые лета, что опровергает мнение, будто тепло всегда помогает. Это и говорит A. B противоречит использованию годичных колец, C не упоминается, D выходит за рамки данных.",t:"The main idea matches what the text actually claims, no more and no less.",t_ru:"Главная мысль совпадает с тем, что действительно утверждает текст, без добавлений.",reviewed:true},
{id:141,section:"RW",unitId:"u-craft",domain:"Craft and Structure",skill:"Text structure",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",p:"Sleep researchers once believed the brain simply shuts down at night. Recordings of neural activity now show it staying busy, replaying the day's events and strengthening memories.",q:"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?",o:["It presents an old belief and then evidence that revises it.","It lists causes of poor sleep.","It compares two sleep studies in detail.","It defines a technical term."],c:0,e:"The first sentence gives an earlier belief (\"once believed\"), and the second gives newer evidence (\"now show\") that changes it. A describes this. The text does not list causes, compare studies, or define a term.",e_ru:"Первое предложение называет прежнее мнение («once believed»), второе — новые данные («now show»), которые его меняют. Это описывает A. В тексте нет списка причин, сравнения исследований или определения термина.",t:"Words like once and now often signal a change in understanding.",t_ru:"Слова вроде once и now часто показывают, что представление изменилось.",reviewed:true},
{id:142,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-alg",domain:"Algebra",skill:"Linear equations & Systems",difficulty:"Easy",type:"mc",q:"If 3x + 5 = 20, what is the value of x?",o:["3","5","7","15"],c:1,e:"Subtract 5 from both sides: 3x = 15. Divide by 3: x = 5. Choice D is the value of 3x, not x.",e_ru:"Вычтем 5 из обеих частей: 3x = 15. Разделим на 3: x = 5. Вариант D — это значение 3x, а не x.",t:"Undo addition first, then undo multiplication.",t_ru:"Сначала уберите сложение, затем умножение.",reviewed:true},
{id:143,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-data",domain:"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis",skill:"Ratios, Percentages & Statistics",difficulty:"Easy",type:"spr",q:"A jacket costs $80. It is on sale for 25% off. What is the sale price, in dollars? (Enter a number)",ans:["60"],e:"25% of 80 is 0.25 × 80 = 20, so the discount is $20. The sale price is 80 - 20 = 60. Equivalently, the price is 75% of 80, which is 60.",e_ru:"25% от 80 — это 0,25 × 80 = 20, скидка 20 долларов. Цена со скидкой 80 - 20 = 60. Иначе: цена составляет 75% от 80, то есть 60.",t:"A 25% discount means you pay 75% of the original price.",t_ru:"Скидка 25% означает, что вы платите 75% от исходной цены.",reviewed:true},
{id:144,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-geom",domain:"Geometry and Trigonometry",skill:"Triangles, Circles & Area/Volume",difficulty:"Medium",type:"spr",q:"A right triangle has a hypotenuse of length 13 and one leg of length 5. What is the length of the other leg? (Enter a number)",ans:["12"],e:"By the Pythagorean theorem, the other leg squared is 13² - 5² = 169 - 25 = 144, so the leg is 12.",e_ru:"По теореме Пифагора квадрат второго катета равен 13² - 5² = 169 - 25 = 144, значит катет равен 12.",t:"If you know the hypotenuse and one leg, subtract: b² = c² - a².",t_ru:"Если известны гипотенуза и катет, вычитайте: b² = c² - a².",reviewed:true},
{id:145,section:"MATH",unitId:"u-adv",domain:"Advanced Math",skill:"Quadratics & Exponential functions",difficulty:"Medium",type:"mc",q:"What are the solutions of x² - 7x + 10 = 0?",o:["x = 1 and x = 10","x = 2 and x = 5","x = -2 and x = -5","x = 5 and x = 10"],c:1,e:"Factor: x² - 7x + 10 = (x - 2)(x - 5). Setting each factor to 0 gives x = 2 and x = 5. Check: 2 × 5 = 10 and 2 + 5 = 7.",e_ru:"Разложим: x² - 7x + 10 = (x - 2)(x - 5). Приравняв каждый множитель к нулю, получим x = 2 и x = 5. Проверка: 2 × 5 = 10 и 2 + 5 = 7.",t:"Find two numbers that multiply to c and add to b.",t_ru:"Найдите два числа, произведение которых равно c, а сумма равна b.",reviewed:true}
);
QUESTION_BANK.push(
{"id":146,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-alg","domain":"Algebra","skill":"Linear equations & Systems","difficulty":"Easy","type":"mc","q":"If 4x − 9 = 15, what is the value of x?","o":["4","5","6","8"],"c":2,"e":"Add 9 to both sides: 4x = 24. Divide by 4: x = 6. Check: 4 × 6 − 9 = 15.","e_ru":"Прибавим 9 к обеим частям: 4x = 24. Разделим на 4: x = 6. Проверка: 4 × 6 − 9 = 15.","t":"Undo subtraction first, then undo multiplication.","t_ru":"Сначала уберите вычитание, затем умножение.","reviewed":true},
{"id":147,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-alg","domain":"Algebra","skill":"Linear equations & Systems","difficulty":"Medium","type":"spr","q":"A gym charges a $25 joining fee plus $18 per month. After how many months will the total cost be $133? (Enter a number)","ans":["6"],"e":"The total is 25 + 18m. Set 25 + 18m = 133, so 18m = 108 and m = 6.","e_ru":"Общая стоимость равна 25 + 18m. Решим 25 + 18m = 133: 18m = 108, m = 6.","t":"In word problems, the one-time fee is the constant and the repeating charge is multiplied by the variable.","t_ru":"В текстовых задачах разовый платёж — это константа, а повторяющийся умножается на переменную.","reviewed":true},
{"id":148,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-alg","domain":"Algebra","skill":"Linear equations & Systems","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","q":"Which equation represents a line with slope 3 that passes through the point (0, −2)?","o":["y = 3x + 2","y = −2x + 3","y = 3x − 2","y = −3x − 2"],"c":2,"e":"In y = mx + b, m is the slope and b is the y-intercept. The slope is 3 and the line crosses the y-axis at −2, so y = 3x − 2.","e_ru":"В уравнении y = mx + b число m — угловой коэффициент, b — точка пересечения с осью y. Здесь m = 3 и b = −2, значит y = 3x − 2.","t":"A point of the form (0, b) gives the y-intercept directly.","t_ru":"Точка вида (0, b) сразу даёт пересечение с осью y.","reviewed":true},
{"id":149,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-alg","domain":"Algebra","skill":"Linear equations & Systems","difficulty":"Hard","type":"spr","q":"x + 2y = 11\n3x − y = 12\n\nIn the solution (x, y) to the system above, what is the value of y? (Enter a number)","ans":["3"],"e":"From the first equation, x = 11 − 2y. Substitute: 3(11 − 2y) − y = 12, so 33 − 7y = 12, 7y = 21 and y = 3. Then x = 5; check: 5 + 6 = 11 and 15 − 3 = 12.","e_ru":"Из первого уравнения x = 11 − 2y. Подставим: 3(11 − 2y) − y = 12, то есть 33 − 7y = 12, 7y = 21, y = 3. Тогда x = 5; проверка: 5 + 6 = 11 и 15 − 3 = 12.","t":"Solve one equation for a variable, substitute it into the other, and check both equations.","t_ru":"Выразите одну переменную, подставьте во второе уравнение и проверьте оба уравнения.","reviewed":true},
{"id":150,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-adv","domain":"Advanced Math","skill":"Quadratics & Exponential functions","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","q":"If f(x) = x² − 4x + 1, what is f(3)?","o":["−1","1","4","−2"],"c":3,"e":"Substitute 3 for x: 3² − 4(3) + 1 = 9 − 12 + 1 = −2.","e_ru":"Подставим 3 вместо x: 3² − 4(3) + 1 = 9 − 12 + 1 = −2.","t":"Substitute carefully and follow the order of operations.","t_ru":"Подставляйте аккуратно и соблюдайте порядок действий.","reviewed":true},
{"id":151,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-adv","domain":"Advanced Math","skill":"Quadratics & Exponential functions","difficulty":"Hard","type":"spr","q":"x² − 6x + 9 = 25\n\nWhat is the positive solution to the equation above? (Enter a number)","ans":["8"],"e":"The left side is a perfect square: (x − 3)² = 25. Then x − 3 = 5 or x − 3 = −5, so x = 8 or x = −2. The positive solution is 8.","e_ru":"Левая часть — полный квадрат: (x − 3)² = 25. Тогда x − 3 = 5 или x − 3 = −5, то есть x = 8 или x = −2. Положительное решение — 8.","t":"Look for a perfect square before expanding or using the quadratic formula.","t_ru":"Ищите полный квадрат, прежде чем раскрывать скобки или применять формулу корней.","reviewed":true},
{"id":152,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-adv","domain":"Advanced Math","skill":"Quadratics & Exponential functions","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","q":"A population of 500 bacteria doubles every 3 hours. Which expression gives the population after t hours?","o":["500(2)^(3t)","500(2)^(t/3)","500(3)^(t/2)","500 + 2t/3"],"c":1,"e":"Doubling happens t/3 times in t hours, so the population is 500 × 2^(t/3). The exponent must count the number of doubling periods, not the hours.","e_ru":"За t часов удвоение происходит t/3 раз, значит численность равна 500 × 2^(t/3). Показатель степени считает число периодов удвоения, а не часы.","t":"In exponential growth, the exponent counts how many growth periods have passed.","t_ru":"В показательном росте показатель степени считает, сколько периодов роста прошло.","reviewed":true},
{"id":153,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-data","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill":"Ratios, Percentages & Statistics","difficulty":"Medium","type":"spr","q":"What is the median of the data set 3, 7, 8, 12, 15, 20? (Enter a number)","ans":["10"],"e":"There is an even number of values, so the median is the mean of the two middle values: (8 + 12)/2 = 10.","e_ru":"Значений чётное число, поэтому медиана равна среднему двух средних значений: (8 + 12)/2 = 10.","t":"With an even number of values, average the two middle ones.","t_ru":"При чётном числе значений возьмите среднее двух средних.","reviewed":true},
{"id":154,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-data","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill":"Ratios, Percentages & Statistics","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","q":"A shirt originally costs $60. It is discounted by 30%, and then the sale price is reduced by a further 10%. What is the final price?","o":["$42.00","$38.00","$36.00","$37.80"],"c":3,"e":"After 30% off the price is 60 × 0.70 = 42. A further 10% off gives 42 × 0.90 = 37.80. The discounts do not add to 40%, because the second is taken from the lower price.","e_ru":"После скидки 30% цена равна 60 × 0,70 = 42. Ещё 10% скидки дают 42 × 0,90 = 37,80. Скидки не складываются в 40%, потому что вторая считается от меньшей цены.","t":"Successive percent changes multiply; they do not add.","t_ru":"Последовательные процентные изменения перемножаются, а не складываются.","reviewed":true},
{"id":155,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-data","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill":"Ratios, Percentages & Statistics","difficulty":"Easy","type":"spr","q":"On a map, 2 cm represents 15 km. A distance of 7 cm on the map represents how many kilometers? (Enter a number)","ans":["52.5","105/2"],"e":"Set up a proportion: 2/15 = 7/x, or use the rate 15/2 = 7.5 km per cm. Then 7 × 7.5 = 52.5 km.","e_ru":"Составим пропорцию или найдём масштаб: 15/2 = 7,5 км на 1 см. Тогда 7 × 7,5 = 52,5 км.","t":"Find the value of one unit first, then scale it.","t_ru":"Сначала найдите значение одной единицы, затем умножьте.","reviewed":true},
{"id":156,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-geom","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Triangles, Circles & Area/Volume","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","q":"A rectangle has a perimeter of 36 and a length of 11. What is its area?","o":["66","72","77","84"],"c":2,"e":"Perimeter = 2(length + width), so 36 = 2(11 + w), 11 + w = 18 and w = 7. Area = 11 × 7 = 77.","e_ru":"Периметр = 2(длина + ширина), значит 36 = 2(11 + w), 11 + w = 18 и w = 7. Площадь = 11 × 7 = 77.","t":"Find the missing side from the perimeter before calculating the area.","t_ru":"Сначала найдите недостающую сторону по периметру, потом считайте площадь.","reviewed":true},
{"id":157,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-geom","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Triangles, Circles & Area/Volume","difficulty":"Hard","type":"spr","q":"The volume of a cylinder with radius 3 and height 5 is kπ. What is the value of k? (Enter a number)","ans":["45"],"e":"Volume = πr²h = π × 3² × 5 = 45π, so k = 45.","e_ru":"Объём = πr²h = π × 3² × 5 = 45π, значит k = 45.","t":"Cylinder volume is the area of the circular base times the height.","t_ru":"Объём цилиндра — это площадь круглого основания, умноженная на высоту.","reviewed":true},
{"id":158,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-geom","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Triangles, Circles & Area/Volume","difficulty":"Easy","type":"mc","q":"Two angles of a triangle measure 50° and 65°. What is the measure of the third angle?","o":["55°","60°","65°","75°"],"c":2,"e":"The angles of a triangle add up to 180°. 180 − 50 − 65 = 65, so the third angle is 65°.","e_ru":"Сумма углов треугольника равна 180°. 180 − 50 − 65 = 65, значит третий угол равен 65°.","t":"The three angles of a triangle always sum to 180°.","t_ru":"Три угла треугольника всегда дают в сумме 180°.","reviewed":true},
{"id":159,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-trans","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","type":"mc","p":"The park offers free yoga classes. ___ it hosts a weekly farmers' market.","q":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","o":["However,","Therefore,","Instead,","In addition,"],"c":3,"e":"The second sentence adds another feature of the park, so it continues the idea instead of contrasting with it or presenting a result. \"In addition\" signals this. \"However\" and \"instead\" signal contrast, and \"therefore\" signals a result.","e_ru":"Второе предложение добавляет ещё одну особенность парка, то есть продолжает мысль, а не противопоставляет или показывает следствие. Это обозначает «In addition». «However» и «instead» — контраст, «therefore» — следствие.","t":"If the second sentence adds a similar idea, choose an addition transition.","t_ru":"Если второе предложение добавляет похожую мысль, выбирайте переход добавления.","reviewed":true},
{"id":160,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-bounds","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Commas","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"The bakery, which opened last ___ already has a loyal following.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["spring","spring,","spring;","spring:"],"c":1,"e":"\"Which opened last spring\" is extra information inside the sentence, so it must be closed with a comma, just as it was opened with one. A semicolon or colon would wrongly separate the subject from its verb.","e_ru":"«Which opened last spring» — дополнительная информация внутри предложения, поэтому её нужно закрыть запятой, как и открыли. Точка с запятой или двоеточие неверно отделили бы подлежащее от глагола.","t":"Extra information set off with one comma needs a matching comma at the end.","t_ru":"Если дополнительная информация открыта запятой, в конце нужна парная запятая.","reviewed":true},
{"id":161,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-form","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Form, structure, and sense","difficulty":"Easy","type":"mc","p":"The second test was more difficult ___ the first.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["that","then","than","as"],"c":2,"e":"A comparison with \"more difficult\" uses \"than\". \"Then\" refers to time, \"that\" and \"as\" do not complete the comparison.","e_ru":"Сравнение со словами «more difficult» строится с «than». «Then» относится ко времени, «that» и «as» не завершают сравнение.","t":"Use than for comparisons and then for time or sequence.","t_ru":"Than используется для сравнения, then — для времени и последовательности.","reviewed":true},
{"id":162,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-craft","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in context","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"Although the critic's review was largely ___, it did acknowledge a few strengths in the film.","q":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?","o":["generous","cheerful","brief","scathing"],"c":3,"e":"\"Although\" signals contrast: the review still acknowledged a few strengths, so it was mostly very harsh. \"Scathing\" means harshly critical. \"Generous\" and \"cheerful\" would not contrast with the strengths, and \"brief\" does not create a contrast.","e_ru":"«Although» указывает на контраст: рецензия всё же признала несколько достоинств, значит в основном она была очень резкой. «Scathing» значит «беспощадно критичный». «Generous» и «cheerful» не контрастируют с достоинствами, а «brief» не создаёт контраста.","t":"A contrast word such as although tells you the missing word should oppose the other idea.","t_ru":"Слово контраста, например although, подсказывает, что пропущенное слово противоположно другой идее.","reviewed":true},
{"id":163,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-info","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","p":"After the city introduced a deposit on glass bottles, the number of bottles found in parks dropped sharply. Officials noted, however, that the number of bottles sold stayed about the same. The data suggest that the deposit","q":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","o":["caused people to buy far fewer bottles","had no effect on litter","changed what people did with empty bottles rather than how many they bought","made bottles cheaper to produce"],"c":2,"e":"Bottles in parks dropped sharply, but the number of bottles sold stayed about the same. So people still bought bottles but handled the empty ones differently, for example by returning them. The deposit did not reduce purchases, it clearly affected litter, and the text says nothing about production costs.","e_ru":"Бутылок в парках стало гораздо меньше, а число проданных бутылок почти не изменилось. Значит, люди покупали столько же, но иначе обращались с пустыми, например сдавали их. Залог не сократил покупки, на мусор он повлиял, а о стоимости производства в тексте ничего нет.","t":"Combine every piece of data; a good inference must fit all of it.","t_ru":"Учитывайте все данные: верный вывод должен соответствовать им всем.","reviewed":true},
{"id":164,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-info","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"A student claims that reading fiction improves empathy.","q":"Which finding, if true, would most directly weaken the student's claim?","o":["Many people enjoy reading fiction.","Fiction books are longer than nonfiction books.","Empathy is valued in many professions.","Participants who read fiction scored no higher on an empathy test than participants who read nothing."],"c":3,"e":"The claim says reading fiction improves empathy. A result showing no difference in empathy between fiction readers and non-readers directly challenges it. The other statements say nothing about whether fiction affects empathy.","e_ru":"Утверждение гласит, что чтение художественной литературы развивает эмпатию. Результат, где у читателей и нечитателей эмпатия одинакова, прямо ему противоречит. Остальные утверждения ничего не говорят о влиянии литературы на эмпатию.","t":"To weaken a claim, find evidence that contradicts the link it describes.","t_ru":"Чтобы ослабить утверждение, найдите данные, которые противоречат описанной в нём связи.","reviewed":true}
);
QUESTION_BANK.push(
{"id":165,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-alg","domain":"Algebra","skill":"Linear equations & Systems","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","q":"The sum of two numbers is 24 and their difference is 6. What is the larger number?","o":["9","12","15","18"],"c":2,"e":"Let the numbers be x and y: x + y = 24 and x − y = 6. Adding the equations gives 2x = 30, so x = 15. The other number is 9, and 15 − 9 = 6.","e_ru":"Пусть числа x и y: x + y = 24 и x − y = 6. Сложим уравнения: 2x = 30, x = 15. Второе число равно 9, и 15 − 9 = 6.","t":"Adding a sum equation and a difference equation eliminates one variable.","t_ru":"Сложение уравнения суммы и уравнения разности исключает одну переменную.","reviewed":true},
{"id":166,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-alg","domain":"Algebra","skill":"Linear equations & Systems","difficulty":"Hard","type":"spr","q":"If 3(2x − 1) = 5x + 4, what is the value of x? (Enter a number)","ans":["7"],"e":"Expand: 6x − 3 = 5x + 4. Subtract 5x: x − 3 = 4. Add 3: x = 7. Check: 3(13) = 39 and 5(7) + 4 = 39.","e_ru":"Раскроем скобки: 6x − 3 = 5x + 4. Вычтем 5x: x − 3 = 4. Прибавим 3: x = 7. Проверка: 3(13) = 39 и 5(7) + 4 = 39.","t":"Expand brackets first, then collect the x terms on one side.","t_ru":"Сначала раскройте скобки, затем соберите слагаемые с x в одной части.","reviewed":true},
{"id":167,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-adv","domain":"Advanced Math","skill":"Quadratics & Exponential functions","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","q":"Which expression is equivalent to (2x + 1)(x − 3)?","o":["2x² + 5x − 3","2x² − 7x − 3","2x² − 6x − 3","2x² − 5x − 3"],"c":3,"e":"Multiply each term: 2x·x = 2x², 2x·(−3) = −6x, 1·x = x, 1·(−3) = −3. Combine: 2x² − 6x + x − 3 = 2x² − 5x − 3.","e_ru":"Умножим каждый член на каждый: 2x·x = 2x², 2x·(−3) = −6x, 1·x = x, 1·(−3) = −3. Сложим: 2x² − 6x + x − 3 = 2x² − 5x − 3.","t":"Multiply every term by every term, then combine like terms.","t_ru":"Умножайте каждый член на каждый, затем приводите подобные.","reviewed":true},
{"id":168,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-adv","domain":"Advanced Math","skill":"Quadratics & Exponential functions","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","q":"For what value of x is 2^(x + 1) = 32?","o":["3","4","5","16"],"c":1,"e":"Since 32 = 2^5, the exponents must be equal: x + 1 = 5, so x = 4. Check: 2^5 = 32.","e_ru":"Так как 32 = 2^5, показатели равны: x + 1 = 5, значит x = 4. Проверка: 2^5 = 32.","t":"Rewrite both sides with the same base, then set the exponents equal.","t_ru":"Запишите обе части с одним основанием и приравняйте показатели.","reviewed":true},
{"id":169,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-data","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill":"Ratios, Percentages & Statistics","difficulty":"Medium","type":"spr","q":"A fair six-sided die is rolled once. What is the probability of rolling a number greater than 4? (Enter a fraction such as 1/2)","ans":["1/3"],"e":"The numbers greater than 4 are 5 and 6, which is 2 outcomes out of 6. The probability is 2/6 = 1/3.","e_ru":"Числа больше 4 — это 5 и 6, то есть 2 исхода из 6. Вероятность равна 2/6 = 1/3.","t":"Probability = favorable outcomes ÷ total outcomes.","t_ru":"Вероятность = благоприятные исходы ÷ все исходы.","reviewed":true},
{"id":170,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-data","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill":"Ratios, Percentages & Statistics","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","q":"The mean of four numbers is 15. A fifth number is added, and the mean of all five numbers is 16. What is the fifth number?","o":["16","18","20","24"],"c":2,"e":"The four numbers sum to 4 × 15 = 60. The five numbers sum to 5 × 16 = 80. The fifth number is 80 − 60 = 20.","e_ru":"Сумма четырёх чисел равна 4 × 15 = 60. Сумма пяти чисел равна 5 × 16 = 80. Пятое число равно 80 − 60 = 20.","t":"Turn each mean into a total by multiplying by the count.","t_ru":"Превращайте каждое среднее в сумму, умножая на количество.","reviewed":true},
{"id":171,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-geom","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Triangles, Circles & Area/Volume","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","q":"A circle has a diameter of 12. What is its circumference?","o":["6π","12π","24π","36π"],"c":1,"e":"Circumference = π × diameter = 12π. (6π would come from using the radius, and 36π is the area.)","e_ru":"Длина окружности = π × диаметр = 12π. (6π получилось бы по радиусу, а 36π — это площадь.)","t":"Circumference is π times the diameter, or 2π times the radius.","t_ru":"Длина окружности равна π, умноженному на диаметр, или 2π, умноженному на радиус.","reviewed":true},
{"id":172,"section":"MATH","unitId":"u-geom","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill":"Triangles, Circles & Area/Volume","difficulty":"Hard","type":"spr","q":"A square has a diagonal of length 10√2. What is its area? (Enter a number)","ans":["100"],"e":"The diagonal of a square with side s is s√2. So s√2 = 10√2 and s = 10. The area is 10² = 100.","e_ru":"Диагональ квадрата со стороной s равна s√2. Значит s√2 = 10√2 и s = 10. Площадь равна 10² = 100.","t":"The diagonal of a square is its side times √2.","t_ru":"Диагональ квадрата равна стороне, умноженной на √2.","reviewed":true},
{"id":173,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-bounds","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Sentence boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","p":"The senator's speech lasted nearly two ___ listeners left before the final vote.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["hours, most","hours most","hours, however most","hours; most"],"c":3,"e":"The text has two complete sentences: the speech lasted nearly two hours, and most listeners left. They can be joined with a semicolon. Using only a comma makes a comma splice, no punctuation makes a run-on, and \"however\" without proper punctuation does not fix the problem.","e_ru":"В тексте два законченных предложения: речь длилась почти два часа, и большинство слушателей ушло. Их можно соединить точкой с запятой. Одна запятая даёт comma splice, без знака получится слитное предложение, а «however» без нужной пунктуации ничего не исправляет.","t":"Two complete sentences can be joined by a semicolon.","t_ru":"Два законченных предложения можно соединить точкой с запятой.","reviewed":true},
{"id":174,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-form","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Verb tense","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"By 2030, the company ___ its factories to solar power.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["converts","converted","will have converted","has converted"],"c":2,"e":"\"By 2030\" is a future deadline, and the conversion will be finished before or by that time. The future perfect \"will have converted\" expresses this. Present and past forms do not fit a future date.","e_ru":"«By 2030» — будущий срок, и к нему перевод будет завершён. Это выражает будущее совершённое время «will have converted». Формы настоящего и прошедшего времени не подходят к будущей дате.","t":"\"By\" plus a future date often calls for the future perfect.","t_ru":"«By» с будущей датой часто требует будущего совершённого времени.","reviewed":true},
{"id":175,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-form","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Possessives","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"The ___ new playground opened last week.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["childrens'","childrens","children","children's"],"c":3,"e":"\"Children\" is already plural, so the possessive adds apostrophe + s: \"children's\". Forms like \"childrens'\" and \"childrens\" do not exist, and \"children\" shows no possession.","e_ru":"«Children» уже во множественном числе, поэтому притяжательная форма образуется добавлением ’s: «children's». Форм «childrens'» и «childrens» не существует, а «children» не показывает принадлежность.","t":"For plural nouns that do not end in -s, add apostrophe + s.","t_ru":"К существительным во множественном числе без окончания -s добавляйте ’s.","reviewed":true},
{"id":176,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-craft","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in context","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","p":"Rather than adopting a rigid policy, the council chose a ___ approach, adjusting its rules as new evidence emerged.","q":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?","o":["hostile","trivial","flexible","secretive"],"c":2,"e":"The council avoided a rigid policy and adjusted its rules as new evidence came in, which describes a flexible approach. The other words do not match this clue.","e_ru":"Совет отказался от жёсткой политики и менял правила по мере поступления новых данных, то есть выбрал гибкий подход. Остальные слова не соответствуют этой подсказке.","t":"\"Rather than\" tells you the missing word is the opposite of the rejected idea.","t_ru":"«Rather than» подсказывает, что пропущенное слово противоположно отвергнутой идее.","reviewed":true},
{"id":177,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-craft","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Cross-text connections","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"Text 1:\nSome economists argue that remote work lowers productivity because employees lose informal contact with colleagues.\n\nText 2:\nA year-long study of two thousand employees found that those who worked remotely completed as many tasks as office workers did.","q":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the claim in Text 1?","o":["By agreeing that informal contact is essential","By arguing that remote work should be banned","By explaining how employees lose contact","By offering data that cast doubt on the claim in Text 1"],"c":3,"e":"Text 1 claims remote work lowers productivity. Text 2 reports a large study in which remote workers completed as many tasks as office workers, which casts doubt on that claim. The other responses are not supported by Text 2.","e_ru":"В первом тексте утверждается, что удалённая работа снижает продуктивность. Во втором описано большое исследование, где удалённые сотрудники выполнили столько же задач, что и офисные, то есть данные ставят это утверждение под сомнение. Остальные ответы текстом не подтверждаются.","t":"Find the exact point on which the second text challenges the first.","t_ru":"Найдите, в чём именно второй текст оспаривает первый.","reviewed":true},
{"id":178,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-trans","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• The Nile flows north through Egypt.\n• It is about 6,650 kilometers long.\n• Ancient Egyptians farmed the fertile land along its banks.\n• Annual floods deposited nutrient-rich silt on that land.","q":"The student wants to emphasize why the Nile was important to ancient farming. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","o":["The Nile flows north through Egypt and is about 6,650 kilometers long.","Ancient Egyptians lived along a river that flows north.","Annual floods on the Nile deposited nutrient-rich silt on the land where ancient Egyptians farmed.","The river is about 6,650 kilometers long."],"c":2,"e":"The goal is farming. Only the third statement connects the river to farming by explaining that floods left nutrient-rich silt on farmland. The others state facts about location or length that do not explain the river's importance to farming.","e_ru":"Цель — показать значение реки для земледелия. Только третье утверждение связывает реку с земледелием: разливы оставляли на полях плодородный ил. Остальные называют факты о расположении или длине, которые не объясняют значение реки для земледелия.","t":"In rhetorical synthesis, choose the sentence that fits the stated goal exactly, not just any true fact.","t_ru":"В задачах на синтез выбирайте предложение, которое точно соответствует цели, а не любой верный факт.","reviewed":true},
{"id":179,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-info","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","p":"Average monthly rainfall:\n• Town X: January 40 mm, July 12 mm\n• Town Y: January 35 mm, July 60 mm\n\nA student claims that Town Y has a wetter summer than Town X.","q":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support the student's claim?","o":["In January, Town X receives more rain than Town Y.","In July, Town Y averages 60 mm of rain, compared with 12 mm in Town X.","Town X receives 40 mm of rain in January and 12 mm in July.","Both towns receive rain in every month of the year."],"c":1,"e":"The claim compares summer rainfall in the two towns. Only the second statement compares July rainfall in Town Y and Town X directly. The others compare winter, describe one town, or say nothing about the difference.","e_ru":"Утверждение сравнивает летние осадки в двух городах. Только второе утверждение прямо сравнивает июльские осадки в городах Y и X. Остальные сравнивают зиму, описывают один город или ничего не говорят о различии.","t":"Pick data that compares exactly the two things named in the claim.","t_ru":"Выбирайте данные, которые сравнивают именно те два объекта, о которых говорит утверждение.","reviewed":true},
{"id":180,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-craft","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text structure","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","p":"The mayor's plan to ban cars from the downtown core drew immediate protests from shop owners, who feared losing customers. Yet when a trial closure was held, sales at nearby shops rose by eight percent, and several former critics asked that the closure become permanent.","q":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","o":["It presents a proposal, reports opposition to it, and then describes results that reduced that opposition.","It describes a ban and explains why it failed.","It compares two cities that tried the same plan.","It defines a term and gives an example."],"c":0,"e":"The text introduces the mayor's plan, then the shop owners' protests, then the trial results (sales rose) that led several critics to ask for a permanent closure. The first option follows this order. The plan did not fail, no second city is discussed, and no term is defined.","e_ru":"Текст сначала вводит план мэра, затем протесты владельцев магазинов, затем результаты пробного периода (продажи выросли), после которых несколько критиков попросили сделать закрытие постоянным. Первый вариант следует этому порядку. План не провалился, второй город не упоминается, термин не определяется.","t":"Trace the order of ideas: what comes first, what changes, and what follows.","t_ru":"Проследите порядок идей: что идёт первым, что меняется и что следует дальше.","reviewed":true}
);
QUESTION_BANK.push(
{"id":181,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-bounds","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Commas","difficulty":"Easy","type":"mc","p":"The store sells fresh ___ and olives.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["bread cheese,","bread; cheese;","bread, cheese,","bread: cheese"],"c":2,"e":"Items in a series are separated by commas, including a comma before \"and\" in the final pair. Semicolons and colons are not used to separate simple list items, and leaving out the commas runs the items together.","e_ru":"Элементы перечисления разделяют запятыми, в том числе перед «and» перед последним элементом. Точку с запятой и двоеточие для простых списков не используют, а без запятых элементы сливаются.","t":"Separate items in a series with commas.","t_ru":"Элементы перечисления разделяйте запятыми.","reviewed":true},
{"id":182,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-bounds","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Commas","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"Although the road was ___ drivers continued slowly.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["icy","icy,","icy;","icy:"],"c":1,"e":"\"Although the road was icy\" is an introductory clause that cannot stand alone, so a comma must separate it from the main clause. Semicolons and colons need a complete sentence before them, and without punctuation the clauses run together.","e_ru":"«Although the road was icy» — вводная часть, которая не может стоять отдельно, поэтому её нужно отделить запятой от главной части. Точке с запятой и двоеточию нужно законченное предложение перед ними, а без знака части сливаются.","t":"Put a comma after an introductory clause that begins with although, because, or when.","t_ru":"Ставьте запятую после вводной части, которая начинается с although, because или when.","reviewed":true},
{"id":183,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-form","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Subject-verb agreement","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","p":"The results of the survey, along with the comments collected last month, ___ that most residents support the plan.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["suggests","is suggesting","has suggested","suggest"],"c":3,"e":"The subject is \"results\", which is plural. The phrase \"along with the comments\" does not change the subject, so the verb must be plural: \"suggest\". The other options are singular.","e_ru":"Подлежащее — «results», множественное число. Оборот «along with the comments» не меняет подлежащее, поэтому глагол должен быть во множественном числе: «suggest». Остальные варианты — единственное число.","t":"Phrases like along with or as well as do not change the number of the subject.","t_ru":"Обороты along with и as well as не меняют число подлежащего.","reviewed":true},
{"id":184,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-form","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Verb tense","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"When I called her, she ___ dinner.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["was cooking","cooks","will cook","has cooked"],"c":0,"e":"The action of calling happened at a past moment, and the cooking was in progress at that moment. The past progressive \"was cooking\" shows this. Present, future, and present perfect forms do not fit a past situation.","e_ru":"Звонок произошёл в прошлом, и в этот момент приготовление ужина шло. Это показывает прошедшее продолженное время «was cooking». Настоящее, будущее и настоящее совершённое не подходят к прошлой ситуации.","t":"Use the past progressive for an action in progress at a past moment.","t_ru":"Прошедшее продолженное время используют для действия, которое шло в прошлый момент.","reviewed":true},
{"id":185,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-form","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Parallel structure","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"The new library is designed to be quiet, spacious, and ___.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["is welcoming","to welcome","welcomed","welcoming"],"c":3,"e":"The list contains adjectives: quiet, spacious, and then another adjective. \"Welcoming\" describes the library in the same way. The other options change the form of the last item.","e_ru":"В списке стоят прилагательные: quiet, spacious и ещё одно. «Welcoming» описывает библиотеку так же. Остальные варианты меняют форму последнего элемента.","t":"Keep every item in a list in the same form.","t_ru":"Все элементы списка должны быть в одной форме.","reviewed":true},
{"id":186,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-form","domain":"Standard English Conventions","skill":"Form, structure, and sense","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"Having finished the exam early, ___.","q":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","o":["a quiet departure was made by the students","the students left quietly","the exam room was left by the students","leaving the room was done by students"],"c":1,"e":"An introductory phrase such as \"Having finished the exam early\" must be followed by the person who did the action. Only \"the students\" finished the exam. The other options put something else right after the comma, which creates a dangling modifier.","e_ru":"После вводного оборота «Having finished the exam early» должно стоять лицо, которое выполнило действие. Экзамен закончили только «the students». В остальных вариантах после запятой стоит другое слово, и получается висячий оборот.","t":"The doer of an introductory action should come right after the comma.","t_ru":"Исполнитель действия во вводном обороте должен стоять сразу после запятой.","reviewed":true},
{"id":187,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-trans","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"Early maps of the coast were often inaccurate. ___ sailors relied on them for centuries.","q":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","o":["Consequently,","For example,","Similarly,","Nevertheless,"],"c":3,"e":"Early maps were inaccurate, yet sailors used them anyway, so the second sentence contrasts with what we would expect. \"Nevertheless\" signals this. \"Consequently\" signals a result, \"for example\" an example, and \"similarly\" a likeness.","e_ru":"Ранние карты были неточными, но моряки всё равно ими пользовались, то есть второе предложение противоречит ожиданию. Это показывает «Nevertheless». «Consequently» — следствие, «for example» — пример, «similarly» — сходство.","t":"Check whether the second sentence goes against what the first sentence leads you to expect.","t_ru":"Проверьте, противоречит ли второе предложение тому, чего вы ждёте после первого.","reviewed":true},
{"id":188,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-trans","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Concision","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","q":"Which choice is the most concise way to express the idea without losing meaning? \"In my opinion, I think that the proposal is not a good one.\"","o":["In my personal opinion, I think the proposal is not good.","It is my opinion that I think the proposal is bad.","I think the proposal is poor.","The proposal, in my opinion, is something that I think is poor."],"c":2,"e":"\"In my opinion\" and \"I think\" say the same thing, so one of them is enough. \"I think the proposal is poor\" keeps the meaning in the fewest words. The other options repeat the idea of opinion or add unnecessary words.","e_ru":"«In my opinion» и «I think» означают одно и то же, поэтому достаточно одного из них. «I think the proposal is poor» сохраняет смысл наименьшим числом слов. В остальных вариантах мысль о мнении повторяется или добавлены лишние слова.","t":"Remove phrases that repeat the same idea twice.","t_ru":"Убирайте обороты, которые дважды повторяют одну мысль.","reviewed":true},
{"id":189,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-craft","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in context","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"The explorer's maps were so ___ that later travelers could follow them without a guide.","q":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?","o":["careless","precise","outdated","decorative"],"c":1,"e":"Later travelers could follow the maps without a guide, so the maps must have been accurate and exact: \"precise\". \"Careless\" and \"outdated\" would make them hard to use, and \"decorative\" says nothing about accuracy.","e_ru":"Путешественники могли идти по картам без проводника, значит, карты были точными: «precise». «Careless» и «outdated» сделали бы их неудобными, а «decorative» ничего не говорит о точности.","t":"Use the result described in the sentence to decide which word fits.","t_ru":"Используйте описанный в предложении результат, чтобы выбрать подходящее слово.","reviewed":true},
{"id":190,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-craft","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in context","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","p":"Though the proposal seemed ___ at first, closer inspection revealed several serious flaws.","q":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?","o":["costly","lengthy","alarming","flawless"],"c":3,"e":"\"Though\" signals contrast: closer inspection revealed serious flaws, so at first the proposal must have seemed to have none. \"Flawless\" fits. The other words do not contrast with \"flaws\".","e_ru":"«Though» указывает на контраст: при ближайшем рассмотрении нашлись серьёзные недостатки, значит, сначала предложение казалось безупречным. Подходит «flawless». Остальные слова не контрастируют с «flaws».","t":"A contrast word such as though tells you the missing word opposes what comes next.","t_ru":"Слово контраста, например though, подсказывает, что пропущенное слово противоположно тому, что следует дальше.","reviewed":true},
{"id":191,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-info","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"A bakery moved its popular rye loaf from the bottom shelf to eye level. Sales of that loaf rose 30 percent the next month, while sales of other loaves stayed about the same. This suggests that","q":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","o":["customers dislike all other loaves","rye bread is healthier than other bread","shelf position may influence which products customers buy","eye-level shelves always increase sales"],"c":2,"e":"Only the position of the rye loaf changed, and its sales rose while the others stayed the same, so shelf position may affect what customers buy. The text says nothing about dislike or health, and \"always\" goes beyond one bakery's result.","e_ru":"Изменилось только место ржаного хлеба, и его продажи выросли, а продажи других остались прежними. Значит, положение на полке может влиять на выбор покупателей. О неприязни или пользе для здоровья в тексте ничего нет, а «always» выходит за рамки результата одной пекарни.","t":"A good inference uses only what the text shows and does not overstate it.","t_ru":"Верный вывод опирается только на текст и не преувеличивает.","reviewed":true},
{"id":192,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-info","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Main idea","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"Although often portrayed as solitary geniuses, many inventors worked in teams. Thomas Edison's laboratory employed dozens of researchers, and today's technology companies rely on large groups of engineers.","q":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","o":["Edison worked alone in his laboratory.","Invention is often a collaborative effort, despite the popular image of the lone inventor.","Inventors rarely share ideas.","Teams are less creative than individuals."],"c":1,"e":"The text says inventors are often pictured as solitary geniuses but many worked in teams, giving Edison's laboratory and modern technology companies as examples. The correct choice covers this. The other choices contradict the text or are not mentioned.","e_ru":"В тексте сказано, что изобретателей часто представляют одинокими гениями, но многие работали в командах, и приведены примеры лаборатории Эдисона и современных технологических компаний. Это охватывает верный вариант. Остальные противоречат тексту или не упоминаются.","t":"The main idea must cover the whole text, including the contrast it sets up.","t_ru":"Главная мысль должна охватывать весь текст, включая заявленный контраст.","reviewed":true},
{"id":193,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-info","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"A health educator claims that regular walking improves sleep quality.","q":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support the educator's claim?","o":["Adults who walked 30 minutes daily reported falling asleep faster than adults who did not walk.","Many adults own walking shoes.","Sleep is important for health.","Some people prefer to walk in the morning."],"c":0,"e":"The claim links regular walking to better sleep. Only the first finding compares sleep between people who walk and people who do not. The others do not connect walking to sleep quality.","e_ru":"Утверждение связывает регулярную ходьбу с лучшим сном. Только первое наблюдение сравнивает сон у тех, кто ходит, и у тех, кто не ходит. Остальные не связывают ходьбу с качеством сна.","t":"Evidence must link both parts of the claim.","t_ru":"Доказательство должно связывать обе части утверждения.","reviewed":true},
{"id":194,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-craft","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Cross-text connections","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","p":"Text 1:\nMany historians believe the library of Alexandria was destroyed in a single fire.\n\nText 2:\nRecords suggest the library declined gradually over centuries as funding fell and scholars left; no single fire explains its disappearance.","q":"Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?","o":["Text 2 provides an example of the claim in Text 1.","Text 2 repeats the claim in Text 1 in simpler words.","Text 2 addresses a different library.","Text 2 challenges the single-event explanation presented in Text 1."],"c":3,"e":"Text 1 says the library was destroyed in a single fire. Text 2 says its disappearance was gradual and not explained by one fire, which challenges that explanation. The other options do not match what Text 2 says.","e_ru":"В первом тексте сказано, что библиотека погибла в одном пожаре. Во втором — что она исчезала постепенно и один пожар этого не объясняет, то есть второй текст оспаривает такое объяснение. Остальные варианты не соответствуют второму тексту.","t":"Decide whether the second text supports, repeats, or disputes the first.","t_ru":"Решите, поддерживает ли второй текст первый, повторяет его или оспаривает.","reviewed":true},
{"id":195,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-trans","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical synthesis","difficulty":"Hard","type":"mc","p":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n• Octopuses can unscrew jar lids.\n• In tests, octopuses learned to solve puzzles after watching other octopuses do it.\n• Most octopuses live alone.\n• An octopus has three hearts.","q":"The student wants to emphasize that octopuses can learn by observing others. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","o":["Octopuses can unscrew jar lids.","In tests, octopuses learned to solve puzzles after watching other octopuses do it.","An octopus has three hearts and lives alone.","Most octopuses live alone, so they rarely meet others."],"c":1,"e":"The goal is learning by observation. Only the second statement says octopuses learned a task after watching others. The other statements describe abilities or facts that do not involve observing and learning.","e_ru":"Цель — показать обучение через наблюдение. Только второе утверждение говорит, что осьминоги освоили задачу, наблюдая за другими. Остальные описывают умения или факты, не связанные с наблюдением и обучением.","t":"Match the sentence to the exact goal, not just to the topic.","t_ru":"Сопоставляйте предложение с точной целью, а не только с темой.","reviewed":true},
{"id":196,"section":"RW","unitId":"u-craft","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text structure","difficulty":"Medium","type":"mc","p":"Honeybees communicate the location of food through a \"waggle dance.\" The angle of the dance shows direction relative to the sun, and its length shows distance.","q":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence?","o":["It disputes the claim in the first sentence.","It gives historical background for the dance.","It explains how the behavior introduced in the first sentence conveys information.","It compares bees with other insects."],"c":2,"e":"The first sentence introduces the waggle dance as a way to tell others where food is. The second explains how: angle shows direction and length shows distance. The sentence does not dispute anything, give history, or compare insects.","e_ru":"Первое предложение вводит «виляющий танец» как способ сообщить, где находится еда. Второе объясняет как: угол показывает направление, а длина — расстояние. Предложение ничего не оспаривает, не даёт истории и не сравнивает насекомых.","t":"Ask whether a sentence explains, supports, contrasts, or gives an example.","t_ru":"Спросите, объясняет ли предложение, поддерживает, противопоставляет или приводит пример.","reviewed":true}
);
/* answer-key balance: move the correct option away from A/B (only questions whose explanations do not cite letters) */
const RO={"1":3,"3":2,"4":3,"5":2,"6":3,"11":2,"12":3,"13":2,"14":3,"15":2,"18":3,"116":2,"128":3,"129":2,"133":3,"134":2,"136":3,"137":2,"138":3};
QUESTION_BANK.forEach(q=>{const t=RO[q.id];if(t==null||q.type!=="mc")return;const ok=q.o[q.c],r=q.o.filter((_,i)=>i!==q.c);r.splice(t,0,ok);q.o=r;q.c=t});
